## Ownership and execution

The lead exclusively owns Git/index, shared docs/register/catalogue, global project
files and dedicated Godot integration. Workers write only their unique per-ID paths
in queue.json; prefab integration is lead-owned. No worker Git operations, shared
brief edits, shared live Blender/Godot sessions or connector configuration mutations.
Source creation uses isolated Blender CLI processes after pinned-version verification.
Sources use named export collections, explicit linked GLB outputs and retained
provenance, measurements, materials, textures and previews. A cube or successful
import alone is not production readiness. Preserve UIDs/import sidecars and saved IDs.

ROOT plus lead plus at most TWO active specialist/review agents is the active limit.
ROOT launched city_lights.01/.02; adopt them without duplicates. Their callback is
ROOT plus direct lead handoff. Later launches are lead-owned with notifyOnFinish true.
On completion, validate outcome then start the next dependency-ready record; reserve
a slot for batch review. Separate agents may be reused for owned fixes.

Ordinary props have a 90-minute initial cap (60 minutes for simple cases); complex
buildings have a 120-minute initial cap. Correct ordinary owned faults within that
budget; retain failure evidence, do not repeat unchanged failures. Exhausted rows
record concrete remaining work and blockers while independent queue work continues.

## Acceptance and review

Record model-source, export/import, prefab, visual/collision/animation checks separately.
Pending gameplay, device, performance or whole-city placement checks stay pending.
Use clean-context independent art-review at exact commits: Sol6.1 medium/high technical
review and narrowly scoped Astra medium visual review as necessary. Supply raw
requirements and exact base/candidate without suggesting a verdict. Fix concrete
findings once, rerun affected checks and obtain same-reviewer disposition after
material changes. Retain complete reports/logs/evidence and reconcile docs every
6–8 substantive family/batch deliveries. Completed TODO removal accompanies actual
resolving changes only. No schedules or heartbeats are needed.

